libethercat1 for Debian
-----------------------

No in-tree consumer: in the 1.0.0 package set nothing links this
library - the ethercat command-line tool is self-contained, and the
host stack drives the master through ethercatctl and the kernel
module. The library is delivered for site application authors who write
EtherCAT master applications against the realtime application interface
(ecrt.h), exactly as libmodbus ships its runtime library independently
of any tool.

Symbols file: this package ships a shlibs dependency only, not a
symbols control file, for the release-1.0.0 cycle. Upstream maintains a
libethercat.map version script, so a symbols file can be added later
for ABI-break detection without a SONAME bump.

